# Lesson figures (local + zoomable)

When the user pastes remote image URLs (Mathpix CDN, screenshots, book crops, etc.) into lesson content:

1. **Always** download with `npm run fetch-image -- '<url>' --dir <section> --name <slug> --alt '...'` (needs network). Prefer `static/img/<section>/`.
2. **Never** hotlink the remote URL in MDX as the primary `src`.
3. Embed with **`<LessonFigure />`**, not a bare `![...](...)` markdown image:

```mdx
<LessonFigure
  src="/img/calculus/fig-13-2-rolle.jpg"
  alt="Fig. 13-2 Rolle: horizontal tangent between x-intercepts"
  caption="Fig. 13-2"
/>
```

4. `LessonFigure` is globally registered in `MDXComponents.js` — no import in MDX.
5. Keep previews compact (default `maxWidth={280}`); users click to open a zoom modal.
6. Update `scripts/fetch-lesson-image.mjs` output already prints a `LessonFigure` snippet — paste that into the lesson.
